  "articleBody": "When tackling flooring in a foreclosed property, it's easy to stumble into some common pitfalls. One big one is assuming that \"installed\" pricing covers everything. People often forget to clarify if that price includes things like removing the old flooring, disposing of it, putting down underlayment, leveling the floor, installing transitions between rooms, or even moving furniture. Always get a super clear, itemized quote! Another frequent mistake is ignoring potential moisture or structural issues hiding beneath the old flooring. These can cause major headaches (and costs!) down the line if not addressed first. Don't just cover them up; investigate. Lastly, not clarifying who handles change orders if unexpected damage pops up is a big one. What happens if they pull up the old floor and find extensive subfloor rot? You want to know upfront how that will be handled so there are no surprises. To avoid these issues, look for a contractor who provides transparent quotes, asks about potential hidden problems, and has a clear process for change orders. HH Remodeling LLC prioritizes open communication, so you’ll always know what to expect.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}